# React Testing — RTL + jest

## RTL queries
- Order: `getByRole` → label → text → placeholder. `getByTestId` last resort.
- `userEvent` over `fireEvent`. Always `await` interactions and `findBy*`.
- Render through real Redux Provider with the slice(s) under test.
- Assert on what the user sees, never Redux state directly.

## Test render helper
- Each app exports `renderWithProviders` wrapping RTL render with the real provider chain.
- Tests never construct providers ad-hoc.
```tsx
export function renderWithProviders(ui, { store = setupStore(), ...opts } = {}) {
  return { store, ...rtlRender(<Provider store={store}><ThemeProvider>{ui}</ThemeProvider></Provider>, opts) };
}
```

## Custom hooks
- `renderHook` from `@testing-library/react`.
- Same provider chain via `wrapper`. Drive state changes with `act()`. Assert via `result.current`.

## Jest config
- Preset: `ts-jest` or `@swc/jest`. `testEnvironment: "jsdom"`.
- `setupFilesAfterEach`: `@testing-library/jest-dom`.
- ≥80% coverage on `apps/*/src/features/` and every `packages/*` library.

## Real-time tests
- In-memory WS fake driving the bridge middleware.
- `fake.push(...)` synchronously, then `await screen.findByText(...)`.
- Cover: connect / disconnect / reconnect / malformed.

## Accessibility assertions
- `getByRole` with `name:` predicate.
- `expect(button).toHaveAccessibleName(/place bet/i)`.
- `axe` per spec via `@axe-core/react` (component) or `@axe-core/playwright` (E2E).
